 "drivingQuestion": "Why may two people not jointly pledge a meal offering?",
 "outcome": "inconclusive",
 "outcomeNote": "The suggestion is rejected; the question continues in the next unit",
 "continuesQuestionOf": null,
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "menachot.104b.7",
   "daf": "104b",
   "sentenceId": 6,
   "he": "אֵין שְׁנַיִם מִתְנַדְּבִין. מַאי טַעְמָא? אִילֵּימָא מִשּׁוּם דִּכְתִיב ״תַּקְרִיב״, עוֹלָה נָמֵי הָא כְּתִיב ״יַקְרִיב״!",
   "en": "§ The mishna stated that «two» people «do not pledge» a tenth of an ephah together. The Gemara asks: «What is the reason? If we say» that it is «because it is written:» “And when an individual «brings» a meal offering” (Leviticus 2:1), in the singular, that is not a proof, as with regard to «a burnt offering as well, it is written» in the singular: “When any man of you «brings» an offering” (Leviticus 1:2). Nevertheless, two people may bring a burnt offering together, as stated in the mishna."
  }
 ],
